course: dictionary
lesson: 15421
title: Stability: steady and safe
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Stability means being steady, so that something does not fall over, move or change suddenly. It can be about objects, lives, families, countries and jobs. «The tower had a wide base, so it had good stability.» The wide bottom kept it steady, and that is what stability means here.
explain: Stability can also mean calm and safe. «After so many moves, the family wanted stability, so they stayed in one home for years.» Here stability means life stays calm and does not keep changing. Look for clues such as steady, safe, calm and not changing.
explain: Check your meaning by putting it into the sentence. «The boat lost its stability in the strong wind and tipped over.» If you swap in balance, it still makes sense, so you have the right meaning. Lost stability means it stopped being steady.
explain: Stability is a noun. The adjective is stable, as in «a stable home». Phrases such as for stability, give stability and peace and stability are common in books and the news.
fact: Stability means being steady and not likely to fall over, move or change suddenly.
fact: In science, stability is how well an object stays balanced and upright.
fact: A wide base and a low centre of weight make a tower or boat harder to tip over.
fact: In everyday life, stability means calm, safe conditions that do not keep changing.
fact: Useful phrases: for stability, give stability, lose stability, and peace and stability.
exercise: «The wide base gave the tower great stability.» What does stability mean here? | Being painted in bright colours | *Being steady and hard to tip over | Being very tall and thin | Being made of glass
exercise: «After so many moves, the children longed for stability at school.» What does stability mean? | Loud music and busy days | *Calm, safe times when things do not keep changing | Lots of new friends every week | Fast travel to new places
exercise: «The boat lost its stability and tipped in the waves.» Which word means the same as stability? | noise | *balance | speed | colour
test: «Prices kept jumping up and down, so the family wanted peace and stability.» What does stability mean in this sentence? | Shopping every day | *Things staying calm and steady, not changing | Jumping up and down | Going on holiday
test: In science, what helps an object have good stability? | A tall, thin shape | A light, empty top | *A wide base and a low centre of weight | A round bottom that rolls
exam: Which sentence uses stability correctly? | «The cat stability jumped onto the fence.» | «The sandwich was stability and tasty.» | *«The bridge was built for stability, so it stays steady in strong winds.» | «I stability my bike in the park.»
